        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital stay of your 86-year-old female patient, admitted on 12/10/2025 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed the exacerbation. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. She was treated with inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout her stay. She responded well to treatment with clear symptomatic improvement. Patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided prior to discharge. I kindly ask you to continue outpatient follow-up and optimise long-term COPD management. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
